+## 4. Synthesis of Bounded Claims & Integration Limits
+
+### 4.1 Survived Claims
+
+1. **Mandatory Notice Generation**: Notice generation in `build.ps1` is mandatory; a failure in `pip-licenses` triggers the `importlib.metadata` fallback; a generator failure remains fatal after cleanup (exit code captured before uninstallation); and `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` and native command preferences are restored in `finally` blocks.
+2. **Exact Notice Staging & Immutability**: All four notice files (`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`, `README.md`, `antlr4-python3-runtime-4.9.3-LICENSE.txt`, `proxy-tools-0.1.0-UPSTREAM-LICENSE.txt`) are hash-checked against pinned values and lock constraints before and after copying; `StageSourceOnly` stages notices without falsely claiming a freshly generated installed inventory.
+3. **Truthful Upstream Provenance**: Upstream notice texts for ANTLR 4.9.3 (including JS-specific MIT text) and proxy-tools 0.1.0 (including the MIT/BSD metadata conflict, placeholder, and trailing text) are preserved without invention or unauthorized license reassignment.
+4. **Lazy Operation Production & Cancellation**: `OperationFacade` generates segments lazily; cancellation acknowledges and halts generation before subsequent reads; post-close access to facades and streams raises `SessionClosed` locally with zero wire operations.
+5. **Handle Adoption & Process Guarding**: Child processes clear handle inheritance (`SetHandleInformation`) and verify 5 file identities before reading 328 bytes; parent guards outlive child termination and empty job accounting; pending I/O terminates at 0; write-open probes fail with WinError 32 during active guarding and succeed with 0 bytes after release.
+6. **Actual Adapter Plumbed to Factory**: The actual `faster_whisper_session`, factory, `_NativePermit` wrapper, and adapter-owned cleanup operate correctly with generated data, adhering to strict phase transitions (protected admission -> reserved binding -> reserved startup -> running after ack), binding an exact 15-field reliability policy with digest `91fd7a45...`, and restoring all service globals.
+
+### 4.2 Remaining Concrete Integration Limits
+
+1. **No Live Model Weights or Audio Transcription**: All observations across groups 2 and 3 executed against 328 bytes of ASCII fixture files (including 60-byte placeholder `model.bin`). No FasterWhisper or WhisperX model weights were loaded; no audio frames were decoded; no VAD or speech recognition accuracy was measured.
+2. **No Full Installer Build**: Notice generation and staging were verified through unit tests and inert PowerShell block harnesses (`Invoke-NoticeStandIn`), not through an end-to-end `build.ps1` execution invoking `ISCC.exe` or inspecting an installed wheel environment.
+3. **No Durable Quarantine or Crash Recovery**: Observations cover normal, clean child process exits and planned cancellations. Interrupted cleanup, process crashes during active I/O, and durable quarantine recovery remain unmeasured.
+4. **Incomplete Native Namespace Protection**: The child process explicitly reports `complete_native_namespace_protection: false`. Complete native loader isolation is not established.
+5. **Unconfigured Production Globals**: Adapter singletons (`RELEASE_AUTHORITY`, `RUNTIME_PROFILE`, `SNAPSHOT_LIFECYCLE`, `RUNTIME_FACTORY`, `ACQUISITION_SERVICE`) remain `None` in production code; `REAL_APPROVAL` remains absent.
+6. **Commercial Pauses In Force**: No legal clearance is granted; website and marketing remain paused; overall product release acceptance is withheld.
